{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you shall teach them.</b> From the root of שן, a sharp arrow. It is known how the arrow is sharpened. Now it appears that the essence of all man's being is service of HaShem, and his service is to know His deeds. The translators translated [it as] 'at the time of Q-Sh,' and we all rely on them." "<b>When you sit.</b> Joined to 'and you shall speak of them.'" "<b>And when you lie down.</b> To sleep, for there is no commandment upon one who sleeps. Now 'and you shall speak of them' — in mouth and in heart."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Onkelos's Aramaic translation of this word using a standard abbreviation; the Aramaic cognate he cites means 'to repeat/recite.' The abbreviation is reproduced literally without resolution."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:34.126303689Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}